+# M10.3 · A freely evolving bound pair
+
+In the two-unit sector the native seam and degree-reference terms reduce, up to an overall phase, to `H = L_moves/2 − 2κ P_adjacent`. Allowed swaps connect all distinct-port configurations. The contrast is 10 for adjacent units and 12 when separated. The observer occupies one echosahedron and returns the occupied internal seam or quiet. Its echo writes the pair flag and the inverse echo restores the state in each terminal branch. A fresh source is released for each read. [Native operator, full-matrix comparison and decoder](https://github.com/FloatingPragma/observer-patch-holography/tree/4fe10f9ac3e81423155fb3ac7baaf0fdb4c0b11c/openwave/interval_echo/row_04/native_check.py) · [Independent sparse evolution](../scripts/m10_3/row_04_check.py)
+
+| Native exposure | Pair records in the home cell, κ = 8 | Exchange only, κ = 0 |
+| ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| 1 | 4,048 / 4,096 | 1,780 / 4,096 |
+| 7 | 4,052 / 4,096 | 1,182 / 4,096 |
+| 37 | 4,028 / 4,096 | 824 / 4,096 |
+
+A changed-law run using the same source and detector rejects at the native persistence gate. Reproducing the older cell-0 experiment gives local probabilities 0.983880525 and 0.149558605 at exposure 150. The source, same-geometry control, complete simulated single-trial records and logic of the simultaneous four one-sided decisions were fixed for the reproduction at planning commit `52a7cfe62adbb9009737b502c65d3c12508aa1c3`. The strongest native lower confidence bound common to these three comparisons exceeds 95.48%. A separate Taylor evolution on a 1/8 mesh and a bound on between-mesh motion using ΔH = 1.5 give a downward-rounded lower bound of 94% on the local probability throughout the finite window. This bounds the ensemble probability at each possible terminal read. [Complete author records](https://github.com/FloatingPragma/observer-patch-holography/tree/4fe10f9ac3e81423155fb3ac7baaf0fdb4c0b11c/openwave/interval_echo) · [Mesh and interpolation code](../scripts/m10_3/row_04_window.py) · [Replay outputs and failing control](../data/m10_3_reproduction.json)
+
